# Crystal Imperium play test: the route mini-bosses (DECISIONS.md D30). Each of the 28 strong
# route trainers loads with its whole team at the player's level cap and plays to a result
# against the prepared six at that cap. They are fought in groups, at the earliest point their
# routes can be reached (the badges below; the Kanto trainers after the Johto League).
# gEnemyParty: 100 bytes a Pokemon, level at +84; gEnemyPartyCount is the team size.
!new_game()
!battle_style_set()
!no_care_packages()
savestate base.ss

# No badges: cap 15
loadstate base.ss
!prepared_team(15, items=True)
savestate cap15.ss
!battle("TRAINER_MIKEY_HNS")
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 4000 B mikey_action_menu
shot 01_mikey.png
expect8 {gEnemyPartyCount} 3 mikey_has_3
expect8 {gEnemyParty+84} 15 mikey_lead_at_cap_15
expect8 {gEnemyParty+284} 15 mikey_ace_at_cap_15
!autobattle("0,0,0,0,0,0")
expectne8 {gBattleOutcome} 0 mikey_resolved
loadstate cap15.ss
!battle("TRAINER_ROLAND_HNS")
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 4000 B roland_action_menu
shot 02_roland.png
expect8 {gEnemyPartyCount} 3 roland_has_3
expect8 {gEnemyParty+84} 15 roland_lead_at_cap_15
expect8 {gEnemyParty+284} 15 roland_ace_at_cap_15
!autobattle("0,0,0,0,0,0")
expectne8 {gBattleOutcome} 0 roland_resolved

